Background

The UNDP Regional Service Centre for Africa (RSCA), based in Addis Ababa, provides advisory, programme and operational support to advance development results at regional and country levels, connecting regional expertise with Country Office needs. Its operational functions cover resource management, planning, internal controls, risk management, compliance, common services and common premises, with a focus on quality service delivery, business continuity, cost-effectiveness and digital innovation.

Within this context, the Operations leads the multidisciplinary Operational Back-Office team covering Finance, Human Resources, Procurement, Administration, ICT and Security. The position provides operational leadership and advisory support to RSCA and RBA thematic and subregional hubs, and works closely with the Ethiopia Country Office on joint operations initiatives. The position contributes to RSCA's objectives by ensuring integrated service delivery, strengthening financial management, internal controls, risk management and compliance, overseeing common premises and shared services, and advancing business-process improvement. This includes workflow automation, management dashboards, data analytics and artificial intelligence to enhance oversight, reduce administrative burden and improve operational efficiency.

The position operates in a complex, multi-stakeholder regional environment, requiring effective coordination across RSCA, RBA hubs, Country Offices, HQ units, UN entities, service providers and other partners. A key challenge is balancing responsive, cost-effective service delivery with robust internal controls, policy compliance and accountability. The role must also navigate resource constraints and financial sustainability pressures, including budget performance, cost optimization, cost recovery and contractual exposures. Managing common premises and shared services requires coordination among multiple participating entities and service providers, ensuring equitable and sustainable service delivery. Finally, the role must anticipate evolving operational risks and maintain effective business continuity and contingency arrangements safeguarding critical operational functions.

Scope of Work

Based at the UNDP Regional Service Centre for Africa, Addis Ababa, Ethiopia, the Operations Manager will lead the integrated delivery of operational services for RSCA and provide operational advisory and support services to RBA thematic and subregional hubs, as assigned and within delegated authority. The work will be performed in accordance with UNDP rules and regulations, the Accountability Framework, the Internal Control Framework, delegated authorities, applicable corporate policies and established performance standards. The Operations Manager will perform the following functions:

Integrated operations leadership and service delivery

- Provide strategic leadership and oversight to the integrated operations team for the delivery of Finance, Human Resources, Procurement, Administration, ICT and Security functions through the RSCA Operational Back-Office;

- Lead multidisciplinary work planning, performance management, staff development and collaboration across operational functions;

- Oversee service quality, timeliness and responsiveness; identify and address operational bottlenecks; and lead the implementation of integrated, technology-enabled solutions, including workflow automation, management dashboards, data analytics and artificial intelligence;

- Ensure that services provided to RSCA and RBA thematic and subregional hubs are client-oriented, cost-effective and aligned with UNDP policies, organizational priorities and corporate performance standards.

Financial resource management, budget planning and cost optimization

- Provide strategic oversight of institutional budget planning, financial forecasting, expenditure monitoring and resource management, including the Institutional Budget component of the Integrated Work Plan;

- Oversee cost allocation, cost recovery, budget performance, financial controls and exception reporting;

- Analyze resource trends, expenditure patterns, funding opportunities and financial sustainability risks, and advise the office senior leadership with evidence-based recommendations;

- Exercise fiduciary responsibility within delegated authority, ensuring that institutional resources are used efficiently, transparently and for their intended purposes, with appropriate accountability, value for money and policy compliance.

Operational risk, internal controls and compliance assurance

- Provide strategic oversight of operational risk management, internal controls, Standard Operating Procedures and quality-assurance mechanisms, ensuring their continued alignment with UNDP corporate policies and accountability requirements;

- Coordinate operational risk assessments and maintain oversight of significant financial, contractual, service-delivery and business-continuity exposures;

- Monitor the effectiveness of internal controls, including ERP approval workflows, reconciliations and exception-reporting arrangements, and advise senior management on emerging risks, control gaps and corrective measures;

- Oversee the timely implementation of management actions arising from audits, oversight reviews and identified control weaknesses;

- Coordinate business-continuity planning and operational preparedness with the Ethiopia Country Office, and promote a risk-informed management culture across operational functions.

Common Premises and Common Services Management

- Provide strategic oversight of common premises, facilities and shared services supporting RSCA and participating UN and non-UN entities;

- Oversee common-services budgeting, expenditure monitoring, cost allocation and cost-recovery arrangements;

- Coordinate and, when designated, chair the Building Management Committee, supporting transparent governance, joint decision-making and implementation of agreed common-premises arrangements;

- Oversee the performance of critical common-service providers and facilities-management contracts against contractual obligations, service-level agreements and quality standards;

- Advise senior management and participating entities on infrastructure investments, operational risks, service resilience, accessibility, safety and cost-efficiency opportunities.

Regional management practice, knowledge management and organizational learning

- Promote operational excellence, policy implementation and continuous improvement across RSCA by facilitating the development, consolidation and dissemination of operational policies, tools, good practices and lessons learned;

- Use corporate performance information, regional networks and communities of practice to identify recurring operational challenges and opportunities for improvement;

- Provide targeted management advisory services, peer learning and capacity-development support to strengthen operational competencies across RSCA, RBA hubs and Country Offices;

- Establish partnerships with relevant UN entities, professional networks and external organizations to facilitate knowledge exchange and the adoption of appropriate innovative practices.

Strategic partnerships and policy engagement

- Contribute in support of the RSCA Head of Operations, to management policy design and implementation consultation mechanisms and relevant dialogues at HQ and agencies forums, including the Bureau’s needs and perspectives on relevant management policies;

- Build positive relationships with external parties, including other UN Agencies, donors, government officials, and external organizations, to tap into innovative approaches and best practices;

- Participate in regional and inter-agency operational forums, UNDP point for the Regional Operations Management Team (R-OMT) under the Regional Collaborative Platform (RCP).

The incumbent performs other duties within their functional profile as deemed necessary for the efficient functioning of the Office and the Organization.

